Keys:
brand
model
year
color
Print:
whole dictionary


only brand


only year


2️⃣ Update a dictionary value
person = {
"name":"Rahul",
"age":25,
"city":"Pune"
}
Tasks:
Change city to "Mumbai"


Add new key "profession":"Engineer"


Print updated dictionary




3️⃣ Delete values
data = {
"a":10,
"b":20,
"c":30
}
Tasks:
Remove key "b"


Print remaining dictionary


🟡 Level 2 — Working with keys(), values(), items()
4️⃣ Print all keys
student = {
"name":"Priya",
"age":21,
"course":"Python"
}
Print only keys.
Expected output:
name
age
course


5️⃣ Print all values
Using the same dictionary, print only values.
Expected output:
Priya
21
Python

6️⃣ Print both key and value
Expected output:
name Priya
age 21
course Python

Level 3 — Logic Building
7️⃣ Count total subjects
marks = {
"science":18,
"maths":20,
"english":15,
"history":17
}
Print how many subjects are present.

8️⃣ Find subject with highest marks
Output should be:
maths
9️⃣ Print subjects with marks greater than 17
Expected output:
science
maths
Level 4 — Nested Dictionary (Important)
🔟 Total marks per subject
students_marks = {
"science": {"internals": 75,"externals":10},
"maths": {"internals": 65,"externals":11}
}
Print:
science 85
maths 76
1️⃣1️⃣ Find subject with highest total marks
Expected output:
science
